Note: that mystery "1" in numberOfSubmissions earlier — with submissions list returning empty. Maybe the user already tested by filling the form! (They asked "check the tally form works" — maybe they tried it themselves and it worked, count=1, but the API list didn't show it... weird.) Whatever — after my playwright test there'll be 2; I'll try to delete mine; if I can't, tell the user honestly.

Also — the earlier count=1 vs list=0 mismatch: maybe list endpoint needs ?limit... it returned totalNumberOfSubmissionsPerFilter all:0. So API says 0 but form header says 1. Possibly a partial submission (started filling, didn't submit — "partial" filter also 0 though). OR the header count is stale/eventually-consistent. Moving on.

Now Playwright captures + end-to-end form test. Write a script:

```js
const { chromium } = require('playwright');
(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const ctx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1600, height: 905 }, colorScheme: 'light' });
  const page = await ctx.newPage();

  // 1. ADDPlus+ light mode
  await page.goto('https://addplus.vercel.app/', { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });
  await page.waitForTimeout(2500);
  await page.screenshot({ path: 'shots/pw-addplus-light.png' });

  // 2. Luminary settled hero
  await page.goto('https://luminarysite.vercel.app/', { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });
  await page.waitForTimeout(3500);
  await page.screenshot({ path: 'shots/pw-luminary.png' });

  // 3. Rewind: scroll through to trigger reveals, back to top
  await page.goto('https://rewindsite.vercel.app/', { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });
  await page.waitForTimeout(1500);
  await page.evaluate(async () => {
    await new Promise(resolve => {
      let y = 0;
      const step = () => {
        y += 400; window.scrollTo(0, y);
        if (y < document.body.scrollHeight) setTimeout(step, 120);
        else resolve();
      };
      step();
    });
    window.scrollTo(0, 0);
  });
  await page.waitForTimeout(1200);
  await page.screenshot({ path: 'shots/pw-rewind.png' });

  await browser.close();
})();
```

